# Implementation Plan: "Lexi Clear" Legal Dictionary Application

Build a modern, responsive legal dictionary application called **Lexi Clear** ("Understand the law, simply.") featuring a Python Flask REST API backend, SQLite relational database, and an educational, mobile-first frontend UI.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Backend & Database Selection**: The backend will be powered by Python 3.10 and **Flask** with a **SQLite** database (`lexi_clear.db`), which runs natively and persistently without requiring external database server setup.
> - **Frontend Stack**: Built with modern, modular Vanilla JavaScript (ES6+), HTML5, and custom Vanilla CSS with Plus Jakarta Sans & Inter typography, Lucide-style SVG iconography, and responsive CSS grid/flexbox layouts. No heavy compile step is required, guaranteeing instant startup and flawless cross-browser compatibility.
> - **Speech & OCR Capabilities**: Real Web Speech Recognition & Speech Synthesis APIs are supported with responsive fallback simulations for offline/restricted environments. The Scan feature includes both real text parsing/OCR extraction and 3 pre-loaded sample legal documents (Rental Agreement, FIR Complaint, Employment Contract) for immediate testing.

